\begin_layout Subsection
Step 1:
 Model the Clock Drift (Linear Regression)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Read your find_sync.T1 files into two arrays.
 Because the sync pulses are emitted regularly by the laser,
 you must find a section where you can match Alice Sync index I to Bob Sync index I + Offset.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Once matched you calculate the drift slope (m) and intercept (c) using floating-point math then apply it to Alice's time domain:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
function Correct_Alice_Time (
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Alice_Raw :
 Bell_Test_Types.Timetag_Bin;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Slope :
 Long_Float;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Intercept :
 Long_Float
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
) return Bell_Test_Types.Timetag_Bin is
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
use Bell_Test_Types;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
