\begin_layout Standard
 How to choose the Window_Bin
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The physical coincidence window for the NIST experiment is generally under 50 nanoseconds.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
To convert 50 ns to your 78.125 ps bins:
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\text{Window\_Bin}=\frac{50\times10^{-9}\text{ s}}{78.125\times10^{-12}\text{ s}}=640\text{ bins}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Set your Window_Bin variable to 640.
 Any events whose corrected times are within ±640 bins of each other are your correlated sequences.
\end_layout

