\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Keep an Eye on the Residuals:
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

After computing the linear regression coefficients (m and c) using the sync pulses,
 calculate the residual error (
\begin_inset Formula $T_{\text{Bob\_sync\_actual}}-T_{\text{Bob\_sync\_predicted}}$
\end_inset

) across the entire run.
 I
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

If the residuals remain flat and close to zero a simple linear fit is perfect.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

If you notice a slight parabolic curve it means that the temperature in the labs caused the clocks to accelerate or decelerate relative to each other and you will need to upgrade your correction to a quadratic fit 
\begin_inset Formula $(a\cdot t²+b\cdot t+c)$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

